# The docker build context is the repo root (see packages/gateway/Dockerfile). Everything the
# builder needs is source, package manifests and the lockfile; everything else only slows the
# context upload down or, worse, would leak into the image.
#
# Patterns are matched from the context root and `*` never crosses a `/`, so anything that can
# appear inside a package carries a `**/` prefix.
#
# Note what is NOT excluded: every workspace package, including the dashboard, the SDKs and the
# examples. `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` compares the lockfile against the projects listed
# in pnpm-workspace.yaml, so hiding one of them from the context fails the install outright.

# Installed and built artefacts: the builder installs and builds inside the image, and a host
# node_modules is the wrong platform for argon2's native binding.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/coverage

# Secrets and local state. Never copy a real .env into an image.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
!**/.env.local.example

# Version control, CI and build-loop metadata
.git
.github
.claude
.ralph

# Test and tooling artefacts
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/playwright/.cache
**/__pycache__
**/*.egg-info
**/.venv
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache

# Documentation and the original starter archive: nothing in the gateway build reads them.
docs
**/*.md
adgate-starter.zip
